  "releaseNotes": "- **`TaskCE.RunOnDedicatedThread`: blocking work an async caller awaits runs on a thread of its own.** For a wait on a synchronization primitive with no async form, which `TaskCE.Run` would park on a thread-pool thread. The pool keeps about one thread per processor and adds more slowly, so each parked pool thread leaves one fewer for every async continuation in the process; a few parked at once, and continuations wait seconds for a thread.",
